16. CONVERSATION-DERIVED VIEWTUBE GOVERNANCE ELABORATIONS
The following points are included as conversation-derived operating context and are not presented as independent verification of repository state.
16.1 Task / quick-win completion
The project conversation established that audits alone are not quick wins or completed tasks. A quick win/task must represent an actual code update, fix, write, implementation, or completed fragment of an established plan.
For implementation work tracked as completed, the project requirement is that the work be merged to main and verified.
This supplements the recovery protocol's distinction between plans, implementation, and verification.
16.2 Recovery and reconstruction
The project recovery work has discussed reconstructing ViewTube from accessible surviving sources, including a donor/recovered repository source. Such sources must be explicitly classified as source/discovery/decision/implementation/design/governance/lost-unverified as applicable.
The donor baseline and recovery knowledge should be preserved rather than silently treated as identical to the original suspended repository.
16.3 Deployment provenance
Render is a relevant recovery/deployment source. Deployment evidence should be preserved separately from repository evidence, and deployment failures should not automatically be treated as proof that the underlying implementation is invalid.
Known Render recovery leads from the shared ledger remain subject to verification.
16.4 UI / Toolbox recovery context
The project discussions distinguish the Toolbox/SubToolbox/UI primitive system, widget/dashboard design system, CSS/design tokens, and the visual reference library.
The sizing system is intended as the default set of sizes used when constructing widget layouts; components and primitives may adapt to other sizes when required by the component's context.
Recovered UI artifacts should preserve their source and status and should not be treated as authoritative merely because they appear in a reference library.
16.5 Canonical-versus-legacy implementation context
Where multiple implementations or compatibility barrels exist, recovery records should distinguish canonical production implementations from compatibility, legacy, alternate, or unverified variants.
The recovery process should preserve the evidence needed to establish which implementation is current rather than deleting historical alternatives prematurely.
16.6 Existing governance over parallel systems
Where an existing ViewTube governance, task-ID, plan, audit, handoff, or consolidation system already exists, recovery should prefer reconciling into that system rather than inventing a parallel permanent index.
The recovery ledger itself remains the cross-conversation coordination bus defined by this document.
